greenhouse:stripe:8176733.full_description:
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are passionate about startups’ success, and building a strong community among founders and investors is core to Stripe’s mission of increasing the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Europe, Middle East, and Africa Head of New Business for Startups, you’ll lead an organization of more than 30 account executives, including three direct-report managers, focused on new business acquisition across the region. You’ll oversee high-value deals, develop systematic approaches to acquiring new business, and establish Stripe as the strategic financial infrastructure partner for high-potential startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead an organization of more than 30 account executives through three regional managers, establishing consistent processes for user acquisition, growth, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Startups New Business revenue targets across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, with personal involvement in strategic deals, deal analysis, complex negotiations, and pricing discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a long-term growth strategy focused on winning new users, increasing product adoption, and improving activation across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement sales methodologies that identify high-potential startups while supporting acquisition across a broader user base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level relationships with key prospects and represent Stripe in strategic deals and at industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailor regional sales approaches for local markets, with a focus on increasing product adoption at the point of acquisition and improving sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Marketing, Solutions Architecture, and Sales Finance to develop value propositions, metrics, and accountability frameworks that support consistent performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of sales experience, including at least four years in second-line management, and experience working with startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and scaling a sales organization of more than 30 people across multiple managers, geographies, and European markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of managing and growing multimillion-euro portfolios, meeting revenue targets, and coaching managers and individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with senior leaders during high-stakes negotiations and complex pricing discussions, and aligning large cross-functional groups around a shared strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify long-term opportunities beyond immediate targets, along with an understanding of how artificial intelligence companies operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

greenhouse:squarespace:8159488.full_description:
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an International Strategy and Marketing Lead to join our INTL GTM team, based in Dublin. This Individual Contributor role owns marketing and go-to-market strategy execution across our European markets, from research and insights to agency partnerships, content, AEO strategy, and channel development. You will be the on-the-ground builder of how Squarespace shows up across Europe, partnering closely with local agencies and cross-functional teams to bring strategy to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on operator who thrives on building, comfortable moving from research and strategic input to managing agency relationships to identifying entirely new channels for growth. You partner closely with the Manager, INTL GTM, and the Challenger Market Lead, translating global strategic direction into local execution across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Dublin, reports to the Associate Director, International &amp;amp; GTM, and involves regular travel across European markets (up to 30%), with a current focus on Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll Get To…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EU Market GTM Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;Own the GTM function for markets across the EU, focusing on identifying the right channels, customers, and messaging to be successful in Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency &amp;amp; AEO Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with local agencies on strategic marketing and AEO decisions, including content placement, on-the-ground research, and event execution across European markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research &amp;amp; Insights: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct on-the-ground market research across Europe, surfacing consumer and competitive insights that inform product and marketing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Channel Identification: &lt;/strong&gt;Work across the organization to unlock new channels and partners to grow meaningfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in Marketing, Brand, Agency, or GTM Strategy at a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing agency relationships, from strategic briefing through execution and performance review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research instincts, comfortable gathering and synthesizing on-the-ground market insights to inform strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in identifying and developing new marketing or distribution channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with significant independence in a &quot;build&quot; role, shaping strategy as much as executing it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-first mindset: personally fluent in using AI tools to drive productivity, with a strong instinct for identifying where AI or automation can improve GTM workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30%, with a current focus on Germany and France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German and/or French fluency preferred, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance with 100% covered premiums for you, your spouse or partner and your dependent children including medical, dental, and vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life and Income Protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility and adoption benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Headspace mindfulness app subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension benefits with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 weeks paid maternity leave &amp;amp; 12 weeks paid paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 weeks paid family care leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Tax-Free Stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee donation match to community organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 Global Employee Resource Groups (ERGs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch and snacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close proximity to cultural landmarks such as Dublin Castle and St. Patrick&#39;s Cathedral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Cash Compensation Range: €56,500 - €86,900 EUR&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary for this position will vary based on job-related criteria including relevant skills, experience, and location, among other factors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to the cash compensation above (which includes base salary and, where applicable for eligible roles, may include overtime pay), Squarespace employees are eligible to be granted an option to purchase our common stock.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Squarespace&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Squarespace is a design-driven platform helping entrepreneurs build brands and businesses online. We empower millions of customers in more than 200 countries and territories with all the tools they need to create an online presence, build an audience, monetize, and scale their business. Our suite of products range from websites, domains, ecommerce, and marketing tools, as well as tools for scheduling with Acuity and creating and managing social media presence with Bio Sites and Unfold. Our team of more than 1,700 is headquartered in New York City, with offices in Dublin, Ireland, and Aveiro, Portugal. For more information about our company, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.squarespace.com/about/careers&quot;&gt;https://www.squarespace.com/about/careers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, more than a million people around the globe use Squarespace to share different perspectives and experiences with the world. Not only do we embrace and celebrate the diversity of our customers, but we also work toward the same in our employees. At Squarespace, we are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of

greenhouse:toast:8226897.full_description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note this is a 12-month fixed term contract.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Toast is driven by building the all-in-one restaurant platform that helps restaurants operate their business, increase sales, engage guests, and keep employees happy.&amp;nbsp;Our PeopleHub team is the heartbeat of our People &amp;amp; Places function, responsible for building global scalable tools, systems, processes, and dashboards that support our employees at every stage of their employee journey. We are helping transform the way that the People and Places Team delivers service to employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the EMEA People Operations Lead you will help build and deliver a frictionless employee experience across the employee lifecycle for our teams in EMEA and help shape a global &quot;shared services&quot; model as it scales. You will own front line support for employee inquiries including benefits and leave administration, alongside other operational activities and program delivery. This role carries real ownership: you are the person Toasters in EMEA come to in the moments that matter, and the person who spots what is not working and fixes it. To be successful you will bring a customer-centric and continuous improvement mindset, a proven ability to use technology and process to elevate the employee experience, strong stakeholder management, and experience in a shared services function within a global matrixed organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the PeopleHub Manager and will work closely with the PeopleHub Director and across our global centers of excellence (COEs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid role requiring 2 days a week in our Dublin office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver front line People Services (Shared Services) support for the EMEA region across the employee lifecycle, including operations, benefits, leave administration, and compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an escalation point for complex EMEA cases, resolving them accurately, compliantly, and with a high standard of service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on metrics and service level agreements (SLAs) to measure service quality and provide insights for decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot what is not working and bring forward ideas to fix it, with the autonomy to test and implement improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvements focused on automation, standardization and scalability that improve the Toaster experience, increase efficiency, and ensure compliance with local laws and customs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with stakeholders across the People Team, Legal, Finance, and Business teams to influence change and drive adoption of an evolving service delivery model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the local subject matter expert who can influence Global COEs on program design that is locally relevant and compliant while aligned to global principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across the People &amp;amp; Places team globally to prioritize and deliver a variety of small to large, complex, integrated People team initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in English&amp;nbsp; and French (preferred), both written and spoken, with the ability to support Toasters and partner with stakeholders in both languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically requires a minimum of 8 years of related experience with a Bachelor&#39;s degree; or 6 years and a Master&#39;s degree; or a PhD with 3 years experience; or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant hands-on experience within People Operations or Shared Services functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a matrixed structure, and influencing outcomes without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with new entity creation and creation of complete employee lifecycle processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Global HR Transformation: strategy, design, and transition of People Operations to create value for the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of labour regulations, GDPR requirements and best practices to help ensure Toast remains compliant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SOX (Sarbanes-Oxley), and experience working within SOX-compliant programs and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of HR Technology, HR reporting, workflow, and auditing requirements (experience with Greenhouse, Workday, and ServiceNow is valuable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem solving and decision making skills with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
