greenhouse:toast:8230767.full_description:
&lt;p&gt;Toast is building the restaurant platform that helps restaurants adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: running the businesses they love. We’ve grown into a leading hospitality software company in the U.S., and are now entering our next phase of growth - one defined by scale, complexity, and a new class of enterprise customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Toast is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Toast Connect team in Dublin. The Connect team owns how everything &lt;em&gt;outside&lt;/em&gt; Toast connects &lt;em&gt;to&lt;/em&gt; Toast including the event infrastructure every team at Toast uses to publish data, the frameworks partners and customers use to integrate through our APIs, and a new charter to make Toast the source of truth for all the data about the customers we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play a key role in evolving our platform to support ever more complex new features and best-in-class monitoring as we scale to orders of magnitude of our current size!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to help create something tangible that is used every day, help businesses achieve their vision, and take on the challenge of scaling a SaaS product, Toast is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, deploy, and maintain scalable backend microservices and RESTful APIs using Java / Kotlin and AWS infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex projects that may span multiple teams &amp;amp; systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion best practices such quality automated testing and phased rollouts to ensure zero-regression releases and high test coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor service health for success &amp;amp; failure, analyze logs and metrics (Datadog/CloudWatch), and participate in on-call rotations to maintain platform uptime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with peer engineers, provide design feedback, and participate in code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with PM &amp;amp; UX on the development of new features &amp;amp; products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor &amp;amp; coach your peer engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling as a genuine part of your workflow, not an afterthought&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years professional backend software development in Kotlin, Java, or another object-oriented language, with solid instincts around testing and code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong understanding &amp;amp; hands-on experience of building RESTful apis, fault-tolerant, highly-scalable &amp;amp; secure distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with sql/nosql databases, strong understanding of distributed datastores and knowledge of when to use what.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with distributed systems concepts, asynchronous messaging (Kafka, Pulsar, or AWS SQS/SNS), and cloud platforms (AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication &amp;amp; problem-solving skills, curiosity to learn restaurant domain workflows, and enthusiasm for collaborating in an agile, cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate humility, empathy and respectfulness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*This is a hybrid role requiring two days per week in the office*&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will help you stand out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing platform APIs that other teams depend on - platform thinking, not just feature delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with document-based or columnar data stores a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring individuals with a wide range of experience so if you have more or less than these exact roles, please still apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we use to make our dish: (Our Tech Stack)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend services which follow a microservice architecture written using Kotlin, Java and DropWizard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event driven messaging &amp;amp; streaming using Apache Pulsar &amp;amp; RabbitMQ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apache Camel for implementing Enterprise Integration Pattern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React &amp;amp; ES6 based Frontend SPAs leveraging Tailwind, GraphQL and Storybook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DynamoDb, Postgres &amp;amp; Opensearch as core persistence data-storage layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Datadog &amp;amp; Sentry for system and application metric and monitoring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Splunk for log aggregation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FireHydrant for alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Spread of Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
