greenhouse:fivetran:8202553003.full_description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;From Fivetran’s founding until now, our mission has remained the same: to make access to data as simple and reliable as electricity. With Fivetran, customer data arrives in their warehouses, canonical and ready to query, with no engineering or maintenance required. We’re proud that more organizations continue to leverage our technology every day to become truly data-driven.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fivetran and dbt Labs are bringing together two industry-leading companies with a shared mission: helping organizations unlock the full value of their data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Together, we’re delivering the data infrastructure layer that helps organizations move, transform, and trust their data — from the moment data moves, through every transformation, to the context teams and AI systems rely on.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fivetran helps organizations automate data movement across the systems, clouds, engines, and tools they rely on. dbt Labs pioneered analytics engineering, helping teams transform data into reliable, governed insights. Together, we support thousands of organizations as they build a trusted foundation for analytics, AI, and better business decisions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As we bring our teams and technology together, we’re building on the strengths of both companies while continuing to deliver the products and experiences our customers know and trust. It’s an exciting time to join us: we’re creating a company with the scale, talent, and technology to help more organizations put their data to work with greater speed, confidence, and impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;During this transition period, you may see references to both Fivetran and dbt Labs throughout our recruiting process as we integrate our teams, systems, and career sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Fivetran scales its Enterprise business, we&#39;re looking for a senior individual contributor – with a strong bias towards AI automation – to own the International Demand Generation across EMEA and APAC. You&#39;ll be the right hand to the Director of Global Enterprise Demand, driving lead generation to ensure we have the touchpoints and MQL volumes needed to hit Enterprise sales targets. You’ll build and run the always-on 1-to-many ABM engine for Enterprise accounts in EMEA and APAC: agent-driven workflows that turn account signals (intent, tech stack, CRM stage) into campaigns, creative, and landing pages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategy-and-execution role: you&#39;ll set the plan and roll up your sleeves with the team to make it work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location and work model: In person in Dublin, Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll co-own the EMEA and APAC enterprise pipeline number alongside the EMEA marketing team, with accountability for lead generation, territory hydration, and the touchpoint and MQL volumes needed to support sales targets. You&#39;ll execute account-specific programs to drive account engagement, lead generation and monitor the funnel from touchpoints through qualified opportunities and pipeline. You will own key paid channels, like LinkedIn and Meta, to drive these outcomes. Things you will build:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic workflows, using Claude or similar harnesses, that creates, launches, and optimizes LinkedIn and Meta campaigns across target-account tiers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connections between ad platforms, Salesforce, and signal sources such as intent and tech-stack data, so audiences and creative update without manual list uploads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A weekly review loop where the system and you assess what worked and improve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work across lifecycle marketing, customer marketing, ABM, product marketing, and regional teams to orchestrate integrated programs. Partnering with the Director of Global Demand and Regional Marketing and ABM leaders, you&#39;ll improve the demand operating model across EMEA and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6 months:&lt;/strong&gt; target-account tiers and signals defined; an agent-assisted campaign workflow live for a first segment, with measurable gains in launch speed and cost per touchpoint or MQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12 months:&lt;/strong&gt; the engine runs across the EMEA and APAC Enterprise account list with BDR handoff, and it improves itself through a regular review loop. Pipeline influence and BDR conversion on engaged accounts are tracked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise in paid media and account-based marketing for enterprise buyers (LinkedIn required), plus experience in at least one of lifecycle, customer, or product marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience running multi-lifecycle stage campaigns targeting enterprise buying committees&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proficiency in using LLM harnesses to automate marketing tasks, and improve marketing performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business judgment and a clear point of view, with the confidence to challenge senior stakeholders constructively and build alignment around difficult tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, specifically in communicating business outcomes, headwinds and tailwinds&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve built and shipped agentic or automated workflows in production, not just prompts: connecting APIs or MCP servers, defining guardrails, and measuring impact. Hands-on familiarity with CRM data (Salesforce), ad platform APIs, and signal tools is a strong plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re comfortable

